  // Enumerator, and the FrozenError waits until that is iterated
  // (`frozen.delete_if` is an Enumerator in ruby; it was raising here).
  // ...and only for a BUILTIN mutator. The name is a stand-in for "this one
  // writes", which it is not for a method someone wrote: ruby raises at the
  // write, so `def zap!; :ok; end` answers on a frozen receiver and an ivar
  // assignment inside it is what refuses. The Set shipped here has a private
  // `__modify!` that raises with ruby's message, and this guard was answering
  // first, about `Object` (`can't modify frozen Object: #<object>`).
